  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantDisclosuresRegardingTheFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-1" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;NOTE 1: BUSINESS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;Principal Business Activity: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Honeoye Storage Corporation (the "Company") is engaged in the commercial storage of natural gas in the Honeoye natural gas field in Ontario County, New York. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The Company is owned by Consolidated Edison Transmission, Inc. (71.2%) and Consolidated Edison Company of New York, Inc. (28.8%), both subsidiaries of Consolidated Edison, Inc.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The Company receives gas from the Tennessee Gas Pipeline Company on behalf of its commercial customers, which it stores in the Honeoye natural gas field, for delivery to their customers. The customers have each entered into a gas storage agreement with the Company under which they have agreed to pay for the availability of the Company's gas storage facilities and delivery capability.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The Company is regulated by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (&#8220;FERC&#8221;). &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The Company is authorized to render two types of storage service: Part 157 storage service, whose rates are regulated by the FERC and Part 284 storage service, whereby the Company is authorized to charge market-based rates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Part 157 contracts are effective until terminated by either party upon 12 months prior written notice to the other party. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;As of December 31, 2025, there are five (5) effective Part 157 contracts. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The rates and the terms of agreement of Part 284 contracts are negotiated between the parties. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;On December 31, 2025, there was one (1) Part 284 contract that expires in 2026, one (1) part 284 contract that expires in 2027 and one (1) part 284 contract that expires in 2030, unless cancelled by either party upon a 30 day prior written notice.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Additionally, there are three park and loan contracts; one expires in 2026, and the other two expire in 2027.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The accounting records of the Company are maintained in accordance with the Uniform System of Accounts prescribed by FERC, which corresponds with accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America (&#8220;GAAP&#8221;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;NOTE 2: SIGNIFICANT ACCOUNTING POLICIES&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;Cash and Cash Equivalents: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The Company considers marketable securities and highly liquid investments with an original maturity of three months or less to be cash equivalents. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;During the course of the normal business cycle, the Company at times maintains on deposit cash balances in excess of the Federal Depository Insurance Company (&#8220;FDIC&#8221;) insured limits.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;As of &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;December 31, 2025,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; balances of cash at financial banking institutions exceeded the federally insured account limit of $250,000.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;Revenue Recognition: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;In accordance with Financial Accounting Standards Board (&#8220;FASB&#8221;) Accounting Standard Update ("ASU") 2014&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Cambria Math',serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;&#8208;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;09, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;&#8220;Revenue from Contracts with Customers&#8221;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Accounting Standards Codification (&#8220;ASC&#8221;) 606, revenues are recognized when control of promised goods or services is transferred to a customer in an amount that reflects the consideration expected to be received for those goods or services. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The Company recognizes its revenue on a monthly storage rental basis.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;NOTE 2: SIGNIFICANT ACCOUNTING POLICIES (CONTINUED)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The Company recognizes revenue based upon rates as provided in its gas storage agreements with its customers. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The Company's rates and assets included in its Part 157 rate-based contracts are subject to review and adjustment by FERC.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Part 284 contract terms and rates are negotiated between the parties. Revenues from the storage of natural gas are recognized when the service is provided. Revenues related to these services provided but not yet billed are estimated each month.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;These estimates are generally based on contract data and preliminary throughput and allocation measurements. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Final bills for the current month are billed and collected in the following month.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Differences between actual and estimated revenues are immaterial.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:11pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;The following presents revenue disaggregated by contract type for the years ended December 31:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Lato',sans-serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:100.000%"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:18.840%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:19.138%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:18.840%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:18.840%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:18.842%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr